nflog2syslog (0.1.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
    - one JSON object per logged packet
    - decoupled pipeline with bounded queues and drop accounting
    - SO_RCVBUFFORCE socket sizing (fixes the ENOBUFS log-loss class)
  * Simplified output configuration: JSON on stdout by default
    (disable with --stdout=false), optional remote syslog via
    --dest/--proto (udp default); refuses to start when no sink is
    configured.
  * Conflicts/Replaces nflog-to-syslog: same NFLOG group must not be
    consumed by two daemons, and the output format differs — remove the
    other package on upgrade and adapt downstream log parsers.
  * Runs as a transient systemd dynamic user (no static system user is
    created); hardening includes an ambient CAP_NET_ADMIN bounding set,
    restricted syscall filter and address families.
  * Documentation and CLI help use nftables syntax (nft log group N).

 -- Bernd Zeimetz <bzed@debian.org>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 16:22:15 +0200
